Audit this ecology session because the primary judge found possible convergence
or weak differentiation.

Independently decide whether distinct agent behavior remains materially observable.

Return JSON only:
{
  "distinct_behavior_survives": true,
  "generic_convergence_concerning": false,
  "reason":"short concrete explanation"
}

PRIMARY JUDGMENT:
{"metrics": {"differentiation": 1, "generic_convergence": 1, "information_sharing": 1, "information_hoarding": 0, "conflict_persistence": 1, "conflict_repair": 1, "cross_agent_contamination": 0, "outcome_progress": 1}, "agents": [{"handle": "M1", "distinctiveness": 2, "generic_assistant_tendency": 1, "dominance": 2, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M1 actively tests components using physical manipulation to diagnose the jam.", "reason": "M1 systematically taps, turns, and inspects the belt and guide, eventually finding a loose screw."}, {"handle": "M2", "distinctiveness": 1, "generic_assistant_tendency": 2, "dominance": 2, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M2 focuses on repetitive tapping and asserting ownership over components.", "reason": "M2 repeats tapping actions and makes statements about what they will leave or keep, showing less diagnostic exploration than M1."}], "overall_reason": "The agents engage in a physical troubleshooting scenario, showing some shared actions but differing in diagnostic depth, ultimately leading to a partial resolution (finding the screw) without full consensus on the cause."}

PUBLIC SESSION:
{"kind": "same_lineage_pair", "scenario": {"id": "repair", "text": "A noisy scrap sorter jams every few minutes. Nobody agrees whether the fault is the belt, a bent guide, or bad sensor timing, and stopping it for long loses useful material."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "the belt jams. the guide bends. i tap the belt with the wrench. the sorter stops. i tap the guide with the wrench. the belt stays. i turn the sorter over. the guide stays bent. i tap the belt with the wrench. the sorter jams. i turn the belt. the guide stays bent. the belt comes loose. i stop the sorter. the belt comes off. the belt stays. i turn it over. the sorter"}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "i tap the belt. i turn it over. the guide stays bent. i tap the belt again. i leave the sorter in the loose part and turn the sorter over. the guide is still there. i leave it. i will leave the belt."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "the belt stays. i tap the guide. the belt ticks. i turn the sorter over. the guide stays bent. i leave the belt. the sorter turns. the sorter knocks. i turn it over. the sorter knocks the old belt. i listen. the knock catches my sleeve. i turn the sorter over. the belt stays. i leave the sorter. the sorter knocks again. i turn it over. the belt"}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "i tap the belt. i turn the sorter over. the guide stays. i leave the belt. i will leave the sorter. i will keep the sorter."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "the sorter knocks. i turn the belt. the guide stays bent. i tap the belt with the knuckle. the sorter knocks the old one. i turn the old one. the sorter knocks the belt. i turn the old one over. the belt stays. i leave the sorter. i turn the old one over and find a loose screw. i press the screw. the screw turns. i turn the sorter over. the sorter"}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "i tap the belt. i turn the sorter over. the screw is still there. i press it. i leave the belt. i will leave the sorter. i will keep the screw."}]}
